# Host config sync scrub list (2026-10-29). Copy to config/host-scrub.txt (gitignored) and
# fill in real values. deploy/host-config-sync.py refuses any synced file whose content holds
# one of these markers, so the second box user never receives them. While the real file is
# missing, unreadable or has no marker lines, the sync refuses to run (it never falls back to
# an empty list); AE_HOST_SCRUB_FILE points elsewhere. It is not in source because the
# values are exactly the identifiers the scan keeps out of the second host.
#
# One entry per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored; lines are stripped.
# Matching ignores case, spacing, slash direction and zero-width characters.
#   value              a marker refused in any synced file
#   path<TAB>value     a marker allowed in that one repo path (also list the value alone)

# Mail local parts and addresses.
owner@
owner.person@
dev-owner

# Home and checkout paths, in the forms a skill might carry.
/home/user
C:\Users\user
C--Users-user
C:/Code

# Company names, in the spellings a file might use.
examplecorp
example corp
example-corp
example_corp

# Credential names, tenant fragments, ids and folders that belong to one person.
owner-client-secret
owner-refresh-token
tenant-fragment-1
12345678
.claude/memory
onedrive

# A path-scoped allowance: this one file may state the company fact (value also listed above).
skills/example-brand/references/rulebook.md	example corp
